# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_self_import_resolve.py" "SELF-IMPORT RESOLVE GATE: PASS" "own-package self-import resolution (recall up, decoy down)" "own-package self-import resolution: inside a PUBLISHED package (a repo with a package.json/pyproject manifest), an import by the package's OWN published name resolves correctly. (a) a self-import SUBPATH (zustand/shallow, from acme.widget import y) STRIPS the leading own-name and resolves the REMAINDER against the package source tree -> a real intra-package dependency edge recovered (measured: zustand RAW recall ~52->56%, 30 recovered edges). (b) a BARE own-name (import flask) resolves to the package ENTRY (src/flask/__init__.py), NEVER a same-basename DECOY (a test-fixture flask.py) -- measured 43 false edges = 17% of flask resolved internal edges, now 0. (c) RECALL-SAFE: a genuine local single-file basename import (a real helper.ts imported as helper) STILL resolves -- the precision fix never over-drops. (d) an EXTERNAL bare import (lodash) fabricates NO decoy edge. CONTENT-FREE: the own name is recovered from the LAYOUT the manifest roots (its path + the src/<name>/__init__ or npm src/ entry), never by reading the manifest body -- only paths + module names cross. A repo with NO manifest is untouched (the own-name logic is inert). Deterministic synthetic fixtures, no DB" "own-package self-import: subpath self-imports resolve to the local sub file (recall), a bare own-name resolves to the package entry not a decoy (precision), a genuine local basename still resolves (recall-safe), and an external bare import fabricates nothing; content-free, manifest-layout-derived" 16
